From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Denis Andreyev <257564291+unsound-mint@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:43:32 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Exact smoothing-term gradient at map edges, log each fit's
 stop reason

The smoothing term is 0.5*lambda*|D x|^2 with D the mirror-padded 3x3
convolution. Its gradient is lambda*D^T D x, but the code applies D twice.
The padding makes D non-symmetric in the two outer rows and columns, so the
gradient is wrong there, by up to 150x in a finite-difference check: every
pixel of the 4x4 level, 44% of 16x16, 0.4% at 2048^2.

The new parameter regul_grad_adjoint = .true. uses the exact adjoint. It
defaults to .false., so existing parameter files give the same result as
before.

Each L-BFGS-B fit now prints iterations, evaluations, final cost, projected
gradient and the stop reason. Before, nothing was printed when maxiter
stopped a level.
